# Test: a command that declares only a summary publishes no long explanation
# VALIDATES: AC-6, the zero-value half -- ze help command --json carries
#            `short-help` and NO `description` key for a command that declares a
#            summary and no long explanation
# PREVENTS: a reader inventing a long form out of the summary, which is what
#           every deleted guess did
# NOTE: this file runs ONE command on purpose. A reject=stdout matches the
#       ACCUMULATED stdout of every command in the file, so a second command
#       here would leave the negative assertion meaningless
#       (docs/architecture/testing/ci-format.md). `ecmp-groups` selects exactly
#       one catalog entry, and internal/component/sysrib/register.go declares it
#       with a ShortHelp and no Description.
# NOTE: the subject was `create interface veth name` until commit fa553a4802
#       (2026-09-03) gave every YANG command node a long explanation, which left
#       no YANG-declared entry carrying a summary and no long form. The
#       assertion below is unchanged; only the command that still has the
#       property moved.

cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=ze help command ecmp-groups --json
expect=exit:code=0

expect=stdout:contains="path": "show ecmp-groups"
expect=stdout:contains="short-help": "Show each prefix the system RIB holds equal-cost paths for, whether or not Ze programs them."

# Nothing invents a long form. The key is absent, not empty. The pattern is
# anchored to the four-space indent of a command entry's own keys, because the
# operator rows further down the envelope carry a `description` of their own.
reject=stdout:pattern=(?m)^ {4}"description":
